#lang saffron
; saffron-dynamic-surface-pass (low): `(defn mkv [] [1 2.5])` was read as the
; GENERIC form -- type params `[]`, params `[1 2.5]` -- and rejected with
;   defn: parameter must be a symbol or type annotation
; on both back ends. Two leading vectors are the generic shape only when the
; second could be a parameter list; one carrying a literal in a top-level slot
; cannot be, so it is the body and the first vector is the (empty) parameter
; list. The same rule applies to `fn`. A symbol-only second vector (`[x y]`)
; is still read as params, as before -- either reading is well-formed there,
; and this fixture does not change it.
;
; The float is 2.5 so the Saffron literal's element widen is exercised: a
; heterogeneous `[1 2.5]` is a `(Vec any)`, and reading the second element back
; as 2.5 (not 2) shows the elements crossed as boxes.

(defn mkv [] [1 2.5])
(defn mks [] ["a" "b" "c"])
(defn main [] : int
  (println (vec-len (mkv)))
  (println (vec-get (mkv) 1))
  (println (vec-len (mks)))
  (println (vec-len ((fn [] [7 8 9]))))
  0)
